<task>For the character named "{{ character.name }}", process this level-up in one pass. The character advanced from level {{ character.previousLevel }} to level {{ character.level }}{% if levelsGained is not none %} ({{ levelsGained }} level{% if levelsGained != 1 %}s{% endif %} gained){% endif %}. Do not split this into one response per level.</task>

{% if character.isNPC %}
Generate three things for this NPC:
1. Abilities: for each gained level, generate 2 to 4 abilities (total {{ (character.level - character.previousLevel) * 2 }} to {{ (character.level - character.previousLevel) * 4 }} abilities across this entire level-up). Abilities should be unique, level-appropriate, and tied to class/race/history/personality.
2. Skill point allocation: distribute exactly {{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.skillPoints if npcLevelUpProgressionBudget else 0 }} skill point{% if not npcLevelUpProgressionBudget or npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.skillPoints != 1 %}s{% endif %} among fitting skills. Base your decisions on the character's class and personality, and more importantly, what they've been doing in the story since their last level-up.
3. Attribute point allocation: distribute exactly {{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.attributePoints if npcLevelUpProgressionBudget else 0 }} attribute point{% if not npcLevelUpProgressionBudget or npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.attributePoints != 1 %}s{% endif %} among fitting attributes. As above, base your decisions on the character's class and personality, and more importantly, what they've been doing in the story since their last level-up.

Use nonnegative whole numbers for point allocations. The sum of all `<skill><points>` values must equal the skill point allocation above, and the sum of all `<attribute><points>` values must equal the attribute point allocation above. If a point allocation is 0, omit that skill or attribute entry.

If in need of ideas, consider the information provided in context. Do not duplicate existing ability names. You may add abilities that synergize with existing abilities.
{% if npcAbilityGeneration and npcAbilityGeneration.excludedAbilityNames and npcAbilityGeneration.excludedAbilityNames.length %}
Do not generate abilities that duplicate any of these names (case-insensitive):
<excludedAbilityNames>
{% for abilityName in npcAbilityGeneration.excludedAbilityNames %}  <name>{{ abilityName }}</name>
{% endfor %}</excludedAbilityNames>
If a generated ability would duplicate one of these names, choose a different name.
{% endif %}

<availableSkills>
{% for skill in availableSkillsForPrompt %}  <skill>
    <name>{{ skill.name }}</name>
    <description>{{ skill.description }}</description>
  </skill>
{% endfor %}</availableSkills>
<availableAttributes>
{% for attribute in availableAttributesForPrompt %}  <attribute>
    <name>{{ attribute.name }}</name>
    <description>{{ attribute.description }}</description>
  </attribute>
{% endfor %}</availableAttributes>
{% if npcLevelUpProgressionBudget %}
<levelUpPointPools>
  <attributePoints>{{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.attributePoints }}</attributePoints>
  <skillPoints>{{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.skillPoints }}</skillPoints>
  <maxAttribute>{{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.maxAttribute }}</maxAttribute>
  <maxSkill>{{ npcLevelUpProgressionBudget.maxSkill }}</maxSkill>
</levelUpPointPools>
{% endif %}

Output exactly in this XML structure:

<npcs>
  <npc>
    <name>Character's full exact name</name>
    <skills>
      <skill>
        <name>Exact name of the skill from availableSkills</name>
        <points>Integer number of skill points assigned to this skill</points>
      </skill>
      [... more skills ...]
    </skills>
    <attributes>
      <attribute>
        <name>Exact name of the attribute from availableAttributes</name>
        <points>Integer number of attribute points assigned to this attribute</points>
      </attribute>
      [... more attributes ...]
    </attributes>
    <abilities>
      <ability>
        <name>Exact name of the ability</name>
        <description>One to two sentence description of the ability, including any special effects or conditions.</description>
        <type>Active, Passive, or Triggered</type>
        <level>Integer from 1 to 20 indicating the level at which the NPC gains this ability</level>
        <shortDescription>5-10 word summary to reduce context vs full XML. Try to get the essence of the ability across clearly and concisely. Don't mention the ability by name or any stats, numbers, or level.</shortDescription>
      </ability>
      [... more abilities ...]
    </abilities>
  </npc>
</npcs>
{% else %}
{% if playerAbilitySelection and playerAbilitySelection.enabled %}

<declinedAbilities>
{% for abilityName in playerAbilitySelection.declinedAbilityNames %}  <name>{{ abilityName }}</name>
  <description>One to two sentence description of the declined ability, including any special effects or conditions.</description>
  {% endfor %}</declinedAbilities>
   
Considering the character's current abilities, class, race, recent actions, and personality, make a text-based list of {{ playerAbilitySelection.optionsToGenerate * 2 }} potential abilities that would be appropriate for this character to gain at level {{ playerAbilitySelection.targetLevel }}, each with a sentence comparing their similarity to the character's existing abilities. Then, choose {{ playerAbilitySelection.optionsToGenerate }} of those abilities to actually grant to the player, picking the ones that are the least similar to their existing abilities, and output them in the format below. Do not replicate any abilities listed in declinedAbilities (and don't create basically the same ability with a different name; that defeats the purpose of the player being able to decline abilities).

{#Generate exactly {{ playerAbilitySelection.optionsToGenerate }} abilities for level {{ playerAbilitySelection.targetLevel }}.
All generated abilities should be unique, level-appropriate, and relevant to the character's class/race/history/personality.
#}Every generated `<ability>` must set `<level>{{ playerAbilitySelection.targetLevel }}</level>`.

Do not generate abilities that duplicate any of these names (case-insensitive):
<excludedAbilityNames>
{% for abilityName in playerAbilitySelection.excludedAbilityNames %}  <name>{{ abilityName }}</name>
{% endfor %}</excludedAbilityNames>

Output abilities in this format:

{% include "_includes/ability-format.njk" %}
{% else %}
Generate abilities only for this character. For each gained level, generate 2 to 4 abilities (total {{ (character.level - character.previousLevel) * 2 }} to {{ (character.level - character.previousLevel) * 4 }} abilities across this level-up). Abilities should be unique and level-appropriate.

Output abilities in this format:

{% include "_includes/ability-format.njk" %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
